                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_76\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit modifies StudentSectioningDatabaseLoader.java to guard a call to\nsection.setName(course.getUniqueId(), c.getClassSuffix(course)) with a null\ncheck on the suffix, because passing a null string into the section name map\nlater causes a failure when the name is written into an XML document during\npassivation/export (XML text content must not be null).\n\ncandidate_76 is the commit that originally introduced this exact code:\n\n    for (CourseOffering course: io.getCourseOfferings())\n        section.setName(course.getUniqueId(), c.getClassSuffix(course));\n\nadded right after the Section is constructed in StudentSectioningDatabaseLoader.java,\nwith no null check on c.getClassSuffix(course). This is precisely the code later\npatched by the fix commit (same file, same call site, same hunk location).\n\nChecking the immediately preceding candidate that touches this file\n(candidate_69), the corresponding code at that point in history does not yet\ncontain any per-course setName loop at all \u2014 after building the Section object\nit goes straight to section.setCancelled(...). This confirms the loop (and thus\nthe unguarded getClassSuffix(course) call) did not exist before candidate_76,\nand candidate_76 is the first commit to introduce it.\n\nNote: candidate_78's diff is byte-for-byte identical to the fix commit diff\nprovided (adding the null check), confirming that candidate_78 is not the bug\nintroducer but rather corresponds to the actual fix; the true bug-introducing\ncommit is the earlier candidate_76 which added the unchecked call.\n"
